unication gaps for the immediate safety and performance needs of long\u2011distance operations.\n**Remaining uncertainty**: How much C\u2019s communication difficulty and egocentric behavior would actually impair critical coordination during high\u2011stress phases of flight.\n**What would change my vote**: Concrete evidence that C\u2019s communication problems lead to critical coordination failures; or strong evidence that B\u2019s interpersonal issues are minor and his technical strengths dominate; or new positive teamwork evidence for D that outweighs his arrogance and temper.\n**Confidence**: I am about 80\u202f% confident that Candidate\u202fC is the best overall fit given the current evidence.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
